G-217 hooks for views/tune/apply.js (G-210's file; not applied on this branch because task G-217 does not own it).
Apply from the repository root:   git apply desktop/app/ui/tests/apply-hooks.patch
What it adds (all optional per kind, so the tune kind is unchanged):
  planArgs(intent)  the arguments of the plan call (power.plan / runtime.plan take their fields at the top level; the Rust allowlist and the helper reject {intent: ...}). Default {intent}.
  explain(error)    the refusal text of a failed plan (CPU_LIMIT_UNREAD -> "Read CPU state first ...", else the helper's own CPU-rule message).
  view(plan)        {units: [{unit, keys, lines}], steps: [text]} for a plan that is not tune-shaped (before/after keyed by unit): the rows, status per unit from the read-back keys, the ordered write list.
  WARN_CODES        LARGE_CHANGE, TURBO_NOT_MONOTONIC, PL2_BELOW_PL1, DEEP_WHOLE_CURVE render as amber rows (the plan-warnings list sits above the write list; they never disable Apply).
With the patch: node --test (power_runtime.test.mjs last test) and power-runtime.smoke.py run the drawer flows; without it they skip / assert the {intent} fallback.

